        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Rhode Island Gulls, United States Basketball League, National Basketball Association\n- People: Manute Bol, Spud Webb, John \"Hot Rod\" Williams, Muggsy Bogues, Robert Rose, Dick Johnson\n- Places: Warwick, Rhode Island\n- Roles: point guard\n\nFacts:\n- The Rhode Island Gulls were a team in the United States Basketball League.\n- The Rhode Island Gulls had notable former players including Manute Bol, Spud Webb, John \"Hot Rod\" Williams, Muggsy Bogues, Robert Rose, and Dick Johnson.\n- Dick Johnson was from Warwick, Rhode Island.\n- Muggsy Bogues was the shortest player ever to play in the National Basketball Association.\n- Muggsy Bogues was 5 feet tall and played point guard for four teams during his 14-season National Basketball Association career.",
